    "summary": "High‑energy show with stellar Eyes > China Doll and a ripping Other One",
    "blurb": "Features an explosive Eyes Of The World into China Doll transition, a powerful The Other One jam, and tight second‑set flow with Bertha > Greatest Story Ever Told. Jerry’s guitar shines, Keith adds jazzy piano textures, and the band maintains high momentum throughout.",
    "review": "The October 29, 1973 concert at Kiel Auditorium captures the Dead in top form during a blistering stretch of the ’73 tour. The first set builds solidly with honky‑tonk numbers before launching into one of the night’s highlights – a searing Eyes Of The World that rolls straight into an immaculate China Doll, showcasing Jerry’s “off‑the‑hook” guitar tone and Phil’s booming bass bomb. The second set rides that wave, opening with a driving Bertha that segues flawlessly into Greatest Story Ever Told, then rockets through Truckin’ into a thunderous The Other One jam where Bill’s drumming anchors the improvisation and Keith’s McCoy‑Tyner‑style piano adds spacey texture. The show rounds off with a joyous Sugar Magnolia/Casey Jones finale, leaving the audience buzzing. Across all available recordings the performance is consistently praised for its high energy, tight interplay, and standout moments that make this night a must‑listen for any Deadhead.",
